            <ArticleTitle>Atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease in systemic lupus erythematosus: the Beer Sheva experience.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>43-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Atherosclerotic disease is common in systemic lupus erythematosus and is the result of multiple pathogenic mechanisms that include traditional risk factors as well as SLE-related factors. Endothelial dysfunction and arterial stiffness contribute significantly to the atherogenic process. Dobutamine stress echocardiogram has not been shown to detect subclinical coronary artery disease; however, the high percentage of left ventricular outflow gradient requires further evaluation and follows-up studies.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
